WEBVTT

00:00:00.723 --> 00:00:02.874
Welcome to the Prac360 support desk.

00:00:02.874 --> 00:00:07.773
This short training shows you how to handle practice queries from start to finish:

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:13.688
tickets, phone calls through 3CX, your schedule, automation, and the numbers your manager looks at.

00:00:14.731 --> 00:00:16.759
The Overview is your start screen.

00:00:16.759 --> 00:00:26.003
At the top you see open tickets, what needs attention right now, our average first reply, tickets solved this week, practice satisfaction and missed calls.

00:00:28.275 --> 00:00:31.347
Below that is your own queue, and the team right now:

00:00:31.347 --> 00:00:37.318
who is available, who is on a call, who is away or on leave, and how many open tickets each person has.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:42.915
Missed calls show here too, so nobody is left waiting.

00:00:42.915 --> 00:00:45.103
One click calls the practice back.

00:00:46.819 --> 00:00:48.840
Under Tickets you see every query.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:54.248
Use the filters for your own tickets, those not assigned yet, or those that need attention.

00:00:54.248 --> 00:00:56.982
The coloured label is the service level clock:

00:00:56.982 --> 00:01:00.310
green is on time, orange is at risk, and red is overdue.

00:01:02.836 --> 00:01:04.528
Open a ticket to work on it.

00:01:04.528 --> 00:01:06.281
On the right are the details:

00:01:06.281 --> 00:01:11.357
status, consultant, priority and category, with the service level for this priority.

00:01:11.357 --> 00:01:14.197
If it is not yours yet, press Take this ticket.

00:01:17.191 --> 00:01:22.078
To answer the practice, write your reply, choose how long you spent, and what happens next.

00:01:22.078 --> 00:01:26.105
The practice sees your answer straight away in their Client support portal.

00:01:28.342 --> 00:01:31.333
Use an internal note for anything only the team should see.

00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:34.424
Notes are marked in yellow, and the practice never sees them.

00:01:37.346 --> 00:01:39.014
Calls come in through 3CX.

00:01:39.014 --> 00:01:45.300
When a practice phones, Prac360 recognises the number and shows the practice and its open tickets.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:51.971
Answer, link the call to a ticket, and when you hang up the call and your time are logged on the ticket.

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:59.359
On the Calls tab you dial out with one click, see every recent call, and connect 3CX:

00:01:59.359 --> 00:02:03.056
add your 3CX address and each consultant's extension.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:08.357
For incoming calls, 3CX opens this Prac360 address with the caller's number.

00:02:10.973 --> 00:02:12.723
Some problems need a developer.

00:02:12.723 --> 00:02:14.191
Press Send to development:

00:02:14.191 --> 00:02:21.136
it goes straight to the Bugs and ideas list in the Admin tool, and the practice sees that our developers are working on it.

00:02:21.136 --> 00:02:25.201
When development marks it done, the ticket and the practice are updated.

00:02:27.597 --> 00:02:29.801
Going on leave, or need a specialist?

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.469
Ask the manager to reassign.

00:02:31.469 --> 00:02:38.379
The manager sees all flagged tickets, and those of people on leave, on the Overview, and moves them with one choice.

00:02:40.831 --> 00:02:43.248
The Schedule shows the whole team's week:

00:02:43.248 --> 00:02:46.843
leave, half days, training, projects and after-hours on call.

00:02:46.843 --> 00:02:52.147
Leave waits for the manager's approval, and automatic assignment skips anyone who is away.

00:02:53.874 --> 00:02:59.429
Automation sends every new ticket to the right team, balanced by how busy each person is.

00:02:59.429 --> 00:03:01.738
Here you also set the service levels:

00:03:01.738 --> 00:03:04.609
how fast we reply and solve for each priority.

00:03:06.755 --> 00:03:10.453
KPIs and reports show how each consultant is doing:

00:03:10.453 --> 00:03:17.777
open and solved tickets, average first reply, service level met, satisfaction, time logged and calls.

00:03:17.777 --> 00:03:20.532
Export it all to Excel with one click.

00:03:22.933 --> 00:03:24.490
Clients is your C.R.M.:

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:30.582
every practice with its plan, contacts, notes, tickets and calls, and its account manager.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:35.920
And this is what the practice sees, in their own Client support portal.

00:03:41.612 --> 00:03:45.452
Under their name, Client support shows all their practice's requests:

00:03:45.452 --> 00:03:48.790
who is helping them, where each request is, and every reply.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:52.963
They can log a request, ask us to call them, and rate us when it is solved.

00:03:55.656 --> 00:03:57.595
That's the Prac360 support desk:

00:03:57.595 --> 00:04:02.748
every query answered on time, every call logged, and every practice kept in the loop.

00:04:02.748 --> 00:04:04.870
Thank you, and welcome to the team.

